@startuml agent-quality-liveness
' ============================================================================
'  agentd - Answer QUALITY + LIVENESS  (decoupled, plug-in / plug-out)
'  Two orthogonal concerns, two DIFFERENT seams:
'    LIVENESS "is it stuck / looping / not moving?"  -> RunObserver port on the LOOP
'    QUALITY  "is the answer good / complete / honest?" -> the verify_answer TOOL
'  Liveness observers attach to the loop (default empty => unchanged). Quality is a
'  normal agent-invoked TOOL: when AGENTD_VERIFY_TOOL is off it is not registered at
'  all -- exactly as if the feature never existed. The loop knows NOTHING about it.
'  Render (from this folder):  java -jar ../../../plantuml.jar -tpng agent-quality-liveness.puml
' ============================================================================

skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "Segoe UI"
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam ArrowColor #555555
skinparam ArrowFontColor #5A5A5A
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #999999
  FontStyle bold
  FontSize 13
}
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #888888
  roundCorner 10
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFF8DC
  BorderColor #C9B458
}

title agentd - Answer Quality + Liveness\nLIVENESS = RunObserver observers on the loop · QUALITY = the agent-invoked verify_answer TOOL (not a loop hook)\ngreen = exists in v2 today   amber = net-new (this plan)   gray = port   blue = tool

' ===========================================================================
' THE LOOP — gains ONLY the liveness observer hooks; knows nothing about quality
' ===========================================================================
package "AGENT LOOP  ·  infrastructure/engine/native.py" #EDE7F6 {
  rectangle "run_agent_loop():\n  stream LLM -> tool calls -> results -> repeat -> FINAL\nLIVENESS HOOKS only (generic, feature-agnostic):\n  • before/after each tool call -> observers.on_tool(ev)\n  • each turn boundary          -> observers.on_turn(i)\nA halt reason injects a steering msg and continues; after STUCK_CAP halts, stop.\nThe loop has NO verifier hook -- quality is a tool the model calls itself." as LOOP #C7B8EA
}

' ===========================================================================
' LIVENESS — observers on the loop (default [] => off)
' ===========================================================================
package "APPLICATION - interfaces/run_observer.py" #E8EAF6 {
  rectangle "PORT: RunObserver\non_tool(ev: ToolEvent) -> str | None   # halt reason or None\non_turn(i) -> str | None     reset()" as P_OBS #E2E2E2
}
package "INFRASTRUCTURE - liveness/   (is it stuck?)" #E1F5FE {
  rectangle "**CallRateBrake** [#3]\nsame tool > N times in the last M calls (ANY args) -> halt.\nCatches varying-arg flailing the per-tool guard can't." as O_RATE #FFE0B2
  rectangle "**NoProgressDetector** [#4]\nK tool-using turns with no NEW result -> halt." as O_PROG #FFE0B2
  rectangle "GuardedTool loop-detection [exists]\nper-tool identical-args repeat + consec-error (complementary)" as O_GUARD #C8E6C9
}

' ===========================================================================
' QUALITY — a normal TOOL the agent invokes; OFF => not registered
' ===========================================================================
package "QUALITY  ·  the verify_answer TOOL (agent-invoked)" #E8F8FF {
  rectangle "**verify_answer** tool  (tools/verify_tool.py) [net-new]\nthe agent calls it on its DRAFT before replying (a plan step);\nreads the verdict as a tool RESULT, fixes issues SILENTLY,\nthen sends ONE clean answer -- no second message, no apology." as T_VERIFY #CFF0FF
  rectangle "PORT: Verifier  (interfaces/verifier.py)\nverify(VerifyContext{task, answer, evidence}) -> Verdict{ok, reasons}" as P_VER #E2E2E2
  rectangle "**LlmJudgeVerifier** (verify/llm_judge.py) [net-new]\nout-of-band judge: completeness / evidence / no-fabrication.\nNeeds ONLY an injected judge-LLM fn + rubric. Fail-open." as V_JUDGE #FFE0B2
}

' ===========================================================================
' PROMPT — completeness self-check (#1, in-band) + verify-step nudge
' ===========================================================================
package "PROMPT LAYER  ·  infrastructure/prompt.py" #FFF4E5 {
  rectangle "**## Before You Finish** [#1] (opt-in)\nin-band self-check: every part addressed + evidence-backed before finalizing." as PROMPT_CK #FFE3B3
  rectangle "**## Verify Before You Send** (auto, only when the tool is present)\ntells the agent to plan a verify step + fix silently, never apologize" as PROMPT_V #FFE3B3
}

' ===========================================================================
' MAIN — composition root: liveness -> engine; tool -> registry; all default OFF
' ===========================================================================
package "MAIN - composition root" #FDECEA {
  rectangle "build_observers(config) -> list[RunObserver]   ([] => off)\nNativeEngine(..., observers=)" as BUILD_OBS #FBD9D4
  rectangle "build_tools(config): if config.verify_tool ->\n  register VerifyTool(LlmJudgeVerifier(build_judge_fn(config)))\nelse: the tool is simply not in the list (feature absent)" as BUILD_TOOL #FBD9D4
  rectangle "config (default OFF):\nAGENTD_LIVENESS = callrate,noprogress\nAGENTD_VERIFY_TOOL = 1   (+ AGENTD_VERIFY_MODEL)\nAGENTD_COMPLETENESS_CHECK = 1" as CFG #FBD9D4
}

' ===========================================================================
' EDGES
' ===========================================================================
LOOP --> P_OBS : on_tool / on_turn
O_RATE ..up.> P_OBS
O_PROG ..up.> P_OBS
O_GUARD ..up.> P_OBS : (related)

LOOP ..> T_VERIFY : the model calls it like any tool
T_VERIFY --> P_VER : verify(draft)
V_JUDGE ..up.> P_VER
PROMPT_CK ..> LOOP : steers in-band
PROMPT_V ..> T_VERIFY : steers usage

CFG --> BUILD_OBS
CFG --> BUILD_TOOL
BUILD_OBS --> LOOP : inject observers
BUILD_TOOL ..> T_VERIFY : register (only if on)

note right of T_VERIFY
  WHY A TOOL, NOT A LOOP HOOK:
  a loop-hook verifier ran AFTER the answer was already
  streamed -> the user saw the answer, then a SECOND
  "I apologize..." answer. As a tool the agent verifies
  its DRAFT first, fixes silently, sends ONE answer.
  Trade-off: agent-invoked (advisory), not loop-enforced.
end note

note bottom of CFG
  PLUG-IN / PLUG-OUT:
  * liveness OFF  => empty observer list => loop hooks are no-ops
  * quality OFF   => verify_answer tool NOT registered => as if it never existed
  * the loop depends on the RunObserver port only; it has ZERO knowledge of quality
  Nothing is coupled: add/remove either via one config flag.
end note

legend bottom
  | Color | Meaning |
  | green | exists in v2 today |
  | amber | net-new (this plan) |
  | gray  | port = interface |
  | blue  | tool |
endlegend

@enduml
